Updated the branch onto current `main` (it was 2114 commits behind) — it merges clean and the change survives intact; I re-checked each anchor on the updated head.

Where this stands against `main` today: the plumbing is upstream now — `InputBatch` takes `logitsprocs_need_output_token_ids` and `_make_sampling_metadata` consumes it (`gpu_input_batch.py:101`, `:903-906`). What `main` still does is approximate the flag with `logitsprocs_need_output_token_ids=bool(custom_logitsprocs)` (`gpu_model_runner.py:730`), so *any* custom logits processor forces the async-scheduling output-token-id repair for every step, whether it reads token ids or not. This PR replaces that with a declared capability: `LogitsProcessor.needs_output_token_ids()`, implemented by the built-ins that actually read ids, and `LogitsProcessors` aggregating it. Nobody upstream has added the declaration side, so the PR is still the missing half rather than a duplicate.

@22quinn @houseroad — one process ask rather than a review request: `pre-run-check` is the only red here and it gates on the `ready` label, so this PR has never had a full CI run. Per `.github/workflows/scripts/run_ci_command.py`, an author can only run `/ci run` once the PR has `ready`, has a trusted approval, or a maintainer has run it once. Could one of you add the label (or run `/ci run` once)? I'll drive it from there. I asked @njhill on 16 Sep but I think it got lost.

